# Byte-for-byte, everywhere. No end-of-line conversion, on any platform.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true by default in Git for Windows, which rewrites line
# endings in the working tree on checkout. Nearly everything in this repo is
# either a fixture whose exact bytes are asserted against or generated data, so
# that conversion is pure risk:
#
#   - samples/*.pdf are binary. Git's text/binary detection is a heuristic, and
#     a PDF "converted" to CRLF is a corrupt PDF and a broken test suite.
#   - samples/*.txt and corpus/files/* are the fixtures selftest, rendertest and
#     the corpus baseline assert fixed numbers about. normalizeText() strips CR
#     before anything measures a character offset, so a CRLF checkout would not
#     actually move those numbers — but relying on that to protect 34 MB of
#     fixtures is a bet with no upside.
#   - data/usc/**/*.json is 63,000 generated files nobody should ever see a
#     whitespace diff in.
#
# `-text` disables conversion while leaving text diffs working (unlike `binary`,
# which also turns diffs off).
* -text
